{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1548738-how-many-gamelines-can-you-crossover-before-it-gets-to-be-too-much","id":1548738,"title":"How many gamelines can you crossover before it gets to be too much?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-23T14:55:13-08:00","id":1548738,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How many gamelines can you crossover before it gets to be too much?","content":"The way I see it there are Major crossovers where PCs and major NPCs are colliding and then there's Minor crossover where a throwaway NPC or monster of the week shows up. Major crossovers I think can cap out at 4 while Minor can go up to 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28699-321rg","name":"321RG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T23:07:56-08:00","id":1548746,"title":"","content":"There's no hard numbers like that. What you want is to be able to settle on a theme and focus for your game, and pick elements that complement rather than detracting from those things.<br /> <br /> If you have PCs of multiple templates, it's essential that the gameplay of the templates fit together in some way, and important that their themes intertwine in some way, so that you can keep all the player characters relevant to the action and to each other. This starts to get hard to do at three or arguably even two templates, though it can be done. For example, you could do a crossover of Changeling and Demon with gameplay focused around managing double lives, brokering deals, and eluding the notice of invisible enemies, and themes of identity, paranoia, and prices paid. Or you could do an on-the-run conspiracy thriller mixing Hunter and Deviant. But you'd have to do a lot of thinking about what compromises you'd need to make to fit a Promethean, with the corporeal powers of their Transmutations and the earthy, introspective themes of their Pilgrimage, into a Mage game that's doing a lot with the Astral Realms and the higher concept cosmic strangeness they mess with.<br /> <br /> If the PCs share a template and you're talking about using elements from outside the gameline, again, that's all about the themes and tone of your particular game. A game about violent renegades holding their turf against threats could take on a lot of different unrelated strangeness as long as it's the kind of strangeness that can somehow be met with violence, whether you're talking about a Werewolf pack, a Hunter cell, or a Geist krewe. A Vampire game about political intrigue and the history of the vampire lineages in the area, however, can't throw <i>too</i> heavily into the mix, or else it's not about the intrigue of vampire lineages at all but rather the intrigue of a number of different weird interacting supernatural phenomena with less personal skin in the game.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, though, the Chronicles of Darkness games are comfortable with having a little out-of-context strangeness thrown in \u2014 the 2e Rulebook, after all, contains general rules for Horrors intended to represent miscellaneous supernatural phenomena not related to <i>any</i> of the gamelines' premises or cosmologies. It's not something for you to avoid so strictly. A Vampire game can still be centered around political intrigue and the history of vampire lineages, even if you discover that part of that history is a subset of those vampires discovering a cave where if you bury an enemy their ghost rises in thrall to your service, even if they <i>survive</i> the burial and claw their way back out.<br /> <br /> Sometimes there's just Mothman, and while Knowing spells are very helpful, knowing about the Supernal Realms doesn't really help mages that much in explaining why now there is Mothman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-24T04:49:27-08:00","id":1548750,"title":"","content":"I think it really depends on the base game. Like, being a vampire doesn't generally give you any greater access to supernatural mysteries than being mortal, and for most of them there's not really much reason to be interested. Mages are addicted to mysteries and have a quasi-academic society based on passing on information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T12:31:38-08:00","id":1548884,"title":"","content":"Ask Samuel Haight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}